     "page": 1,
     "text": "Edwards Group Medical Group\n\nRe: Connor Ellis (DOB 05/27/1969)\n\nDear Underwriter,\n\nI hope this letter finds you well. I am writing to provide a medical summary for Mr. Connor Ellis, who was seen in my practice on several occasions regarding his Anemia / blood disorders. \n\nOn February 10, 2025, Mr. Ellis visited for follow-up regarding his Anemia / blood disorders. During this visit, his blood pressure was noted at 115/79, and his weight was 152 pounds. Mr. Ellis continues to manage his Anemia, which includes venous thromboembolism (VTE) related to Factor V Leiden mutation. Currently, there are no active issues, and his condition remains controlled.\n\nThe previous visit, on May 31, Z024, was also for follow-up on his Anemia / blood disorders. At that time, his blood pressure was 107/85, and he weighed 158 pounds. Mr. Ellis reported feeling well and adhering to his treatment regimen. His anemia has remained stable, and he continues to be monitored closely.\n\nFurther back, on September 18, 2023, Mr. Ellis was seen for similar reasons. His blood pressure on day was 108/85, and his weight was 150 pounds. Mr. Ellis was doing well, with no complications noted in his anemia management. \n\nMr. maintains an active lifestyle, running 3-4 times per week, which is a commendable effort. Regarding his social habits, he consumes alcohol at a rate of approximately 4 drinks per week. He has never documented tobacco use in his records. \n\nAdditionally, Mr. Ellis's family history includes significant cardiovascular events. His father had a myocardial infarction (MI), although the exact age at onset is not documented, and he passed away at the age of 47. His mother experienced sudden cardiac death at the age of 42. Both parents are deceased.\n\nThroughout his visits, Mr. Ellis has been compliant with his treatment plan, and there been no issues with adherence to his medication regimen, although currently, no specific medications are being prescribed for his anemia.\n\nMr. Ellis's physical examinations during these visits have been routine, with no significant abnormalities noted other than those directly related to his known condition. His vital signs have been within normal ranges, and there were no unrelated minor complaints during these you for considering this information. Should you need any further details or have additional questions, please do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Wanda Peterson \nFamily Medicine Group Medical Group\n"
    }
   ],
